  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="6.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIIAtr">III Atr</ref> 6.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6.2" corresp="#wit-h">⁊ gif he þæt ordal forfleo, gilde se borh hine be his were.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="6.2" corresp="#wit-q">Et si fugiet ab ordalio, reddat eum plegius wera sua.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="6.2" corresp="#wit-h">⁊ gif he þæt ordal forfleo, gilde se borh hine be his were.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-h">And if he (the accused) flees from the ordeal, his surety shall pay for him to the amount of his [the fugitive's] wergeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und wenn [Beklagt]er dem Ordal entflieht, so entgelte ihn [sein] Bürge durch sein [des Flüchtlings] Wergeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if [the accused] flees from the ordeal, let [his] surety pay for him with his [the fugitive's] wergild.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares I Atr 1.7.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
